This is how you run this program.

I have two python files: 
one that loads the data (I put this in the scripts: load_data.py)
one that is the main app (main.py) which shows these following data when you run:
- Repeating patrons
- Total renewals
- Most Active Patron

Python packages to install: pandas and mysql-connector-python

To run this program:
- load up sifls2026.sql on Workbench. You should have four tables( )
- I used PyCharm as my IDE and for both python files, add your password from environment variable: In PyCharm go to: Run -> Edit Configuration -> In Environment Variable, type in SQL_PASSWORD=yourpassword (add your password here)
- Turn the SFPL data set from excel to csv and then add it to the pycharm folder that you are running the python files with
- Load data once: run load_data.py
- Run main.py to find the results
